  "question": {
    "text": "A diatomic gas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo></math> does <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of work when it is expanded isobarically. The heat given to the gas in the process is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>850</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>800</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>",
