  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For degree of freedom, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>For isobaric process, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>nR</mi><mi>Δ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>.</p><p>Now, we can write</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>nRΔT</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>700</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p>"
  }
